```python
def hashish(node) -> bool:  # recursively check source segment for hash-ish token
    seg = ast.get_source_segment(src, node) or ''
    return bool(re.search(r'(?i)(sha|hash|digest|checksum)', seg))
```
Careful: source segment for a large expression may include unrelated hash text. Restrict depth: check the direct Name/Attribute/Subscript/Call node's own segment.

Simpler approach: iterate over all Compare nodes and all Call nodes with method names in {'startswith','endswith','find','__contains__','index'} where receiver source is hash-ish; for Compare classify based on operator and operand shape:

```python
for node in ast.walk(tree):
    if isinstance(node, ast.Compare):
        op = node.ops[0]
        left = node.left; right = node.comparators[0] if node.comparators else None
        operands = [left, right]
        h = [o for o in operands if hashish(o)]
        if not h: continue
        seg = ast.get_source_segment(src, node)
        if isinstance(op, (ast.In, ast.NotIn)):
            kind='SUBSTRING'
        elif isinstance(op, (ast.Eq, ast.NotEq)):
            truncated = any(isinstance(o, ast.Subscript) and isinstance(o.slice, ast.Slice) and o.slice.upper is not None for o in h)
            truncated = truncated or bool(re.search(r'\[:\s*\d+\]', seg))
            kind = 'PREFIX' if truncated else 'EXACT'
        else: kind='OTHER'
```
Note: Eq comparisons where both sides are `Optional[str]`: exact.

